[0.044, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m\u001b[2m 56 \u001b[22m **Balance**:\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m  \u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 53 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mA Member's net position in a Group: what they are owed minus what they owe. The Balances of all a Group's Members always add up to exactly zero.     \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 57 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mA Member's net position in a Group: what they are owed minus what they owe. \u001b[48;2;4;71;0mPositive means they are owed money. \u001b[48;2;2;40;0mThe Balances of all a Group's Members\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m    +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m always add up to exactly zero.                                                                                                                      \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[2m 58 \u001b[22m _Avoid_: Debt, total, net\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m  \u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m\u001b[2m 59 \u001b[22m \u001b[12G\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B   \u001b[38;2;248;248;242m\u001b[2m 60 \u001b[22m **Settle-up**:\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[39mUpdated \u001b[1mdocs/adr/0002-integer-minor-unit"]
[0.001, "o", "s-with-remainder-rule.md\u001b[71G\u001b[22m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m(+1 -1)\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;248;248;242m\u001b[2m 1 \u001b[22m # Money is stored as integer minor units; equal-split Remainders go to Participants by a deterministic rule\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;248;248;242m\u001b[2m 2 \u001b[22m \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B   \u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 3 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m\"Exact, no rounding errors\" can be met either with rational Balances (e.g. 1000/3 cents) or with whole-minor-unit Shares that add up exactly to the Am\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m   -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mount. We chose integer minor units. Nobody can pay a fraction of a cent, so rational Balances would only push the rounding problem into Settle-up. Ins\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m   -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mtead, each Expense splits into whole-unit Shares, and its Remainder is handed out one unit at a time \u001b[48;2;92;2;0mby\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m \u001b[48;2;92;2;0ma\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m \u001b[48;2;92;2;0mdeterministic\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m \u001b[48;2;92;2;0mrule\u001b[48;2;61;1"]
[0.001, "o", ";0m. As a result, every Expen\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m   -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mse's Shares add up exactly to its Amount, and every Group's Balances add up exactly to zero. Changing the Remainder rule later would change historical\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m   -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m Balances, so it is treated as fixed.                                                                                                                 \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 3 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m\"Exact, no rounding errors\" can be met either with rational Balances (e.g. 1000/3 cents) or with whole-minor-unit Shares that add up exactly to the Am\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m   +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mount. We chose integer minor units. Nobody can pay a fraction of a cent, so rational Balances would only push the rounding problem into Settle-up. Ins\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m   +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mtead, each Expe"]
[0.002, "o", "nse splits into whole-unit Shares, and its Remainder is handed out one unit at a time \u001b[48;2;4;71;0mto\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m \u001b[48;2;4;71;0mthe\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m \u001b[48;2;4;71;0mParticipants\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m \u001b[48;2;4;71;0min the order they joined the \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m   +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m\u001b[48;2;4;71;0mGroup\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m. \u001b[48;2;4;71;0mWe use join order rather than the order in the request, so the same Expense always gives the same Shares. \u001b[48;2;2;40;0mAs a result, every Expense's Shares a\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m   +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mdd up exactly to its Amount, and every Group's Balances add up exactly to zero. Changing the Remainder rule later would change historical Balances, so\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m  \u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m   +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m it is treated as fixed.                                                                                                                              \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[39mUpdated\u001b[14G\u001b[1mpocock-1.cast\u001b[28G\u001b[22m"]
