[0.001, "o", "8;2;248;248;242m\u001b[2m8\u001b[10G\u001b[22mWhe\u001b[14G a group of\u001b[26Gpeople share co\u001b[42Gts (a trip, a flat, a dinner), working out who owes whom quickly ge\u001b[110Gs messy.\u001b[119GDifferent\u001b[129Gpeople\u001b[136Gpay for diff\u001b[150Gent thing\r\u001b[9C\u001b[1B, and not every expense inv\u001b[38Glves everyone. Splitting by hand produces fraction\u001b[90Gof a cent\u001b[100Gt\u001b[102Gat d\u001b[107Gn't ad\u001b[114G up, so totals drift. Even\u001b[141Gw\u001b[143Gen\u001b[146Geveryone knows\r\u001b[7C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m \u001b[10G\u001b[22m their net position, it's not obvious how to square up with as few transfers as possible. The group needs a single source of truth that records who pa\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 9\u001b[10G\u001b[22m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m\u001b[2m 10 \u001b[22m## Solution\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m… +194 lines \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[3G\u001b[39mI've written\u001b[16Gthe\u001b[20Gspec\u001b[25Gto\u001b[28G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mdocs/specs/0001-expense-splitting-api.md\u001b[69G\u001b[39mand\u001b[73Glabelled\u001b[82Git\u001b[85G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mready-for-agent\u001b[101G\u001b[39min\u001b[104Gits\u001b[108Gheader.\u001b[116GIt's\u001b[121Ga\u001b[123Glocal\u001b[129Gfile\u001b[134Gbecau"]
